  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, and `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` passes (47 passed, 2 skipped).\n\n- **Class:** it sits right after `UUIDParameterType` in `src/click/types.py`, with `name = \"key_value\"`. It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`. An empty value is allowed, so `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Errors:** input without `=` or with an empty key fails through `self.fail(...)` with `'...' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Export:** the class itself, not an instance, is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests:** two parametrized tests in `tests/test_types.py` use `@click.option(\"--set\", type=click.KeyValue())`. They cover valid pairs, including `a=b=c` and `a=`, and invalid inputs (`abc`, empty string, `=value`). Invalid inputs must exit with code 2 and the expected message.\n\nI only ran `tests/test_types.py`, not the full suite.",
